{"agent":"bgp","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new regression never fails on the unfixed router when validation order or a bad id swallows the advertised failure. `_call(..., action=\"fixed\", id=\"B-no-such\", no_task=True)` then asserts only that the substring `\"unknown argument\"` is absent from `text`. A response such as \"no such bug B-no-such\" (id checked first), an empty `text` with the refusal in `_err`, or any other wording that is not that exact phrase all satisfy the assert, so Bab813498a3 stays open while the test is green. It also does not check that `fixed` accepted `no_task` and filed no task; absence of one error string is not that contract. The diff contains no schema or handler change that would add `no_task` to the known-argument list, so nothing here closes the bug the test claims to pin.","digest":"6430f50b331b4c07","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_mcp_family_route.py:test_bug_fixed_takes_the_no_task_argument_the_family_advertises","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_mcp_family_route.py:test_bug_fixed_takes_the_no_task_argument_the_family_advertises"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":965,"diff_sha":"c6605bc60d3c95b63600f793ee5b84375ce9b9860a187e0d48fe0e1b410a44f1","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bab813498a3","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":48.1,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"20610e60a15f3664","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bab813498a3.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261109T100850Z-857994c4.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"e61e5d4c3726","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"86b0e60e361bd80a5ff5124728239dc5c314bf36","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_mcp_family_route.py":"100644 391c2b5037049424a8041ea